## 1. §171 with `g=0.00109`

Put

\[
C_{146}:={4\over9}(\pi+\sqrt{\Delta_2}).
\]

Audited §171 proves that any Type-II subsequential limit

\[
t=\lim {q-k\over D},
\qquad
\delta=\lim {b-P_F\over D}\ge0
\]

must satisfy

\[
F_t(\delta):=
10t-5\pi-5\delta
+\bigl(81(\pi+\delta)^2\delta\bigr)^{1/3}
-{8\Delta_2\over {9t\over2}-2\pi-2\delta}
\ge0,
\tag{PC109.5}
\]

with feasible detour interval

\[
0\le\delta\le
{{9\over2}(t-C_{146})-g\over2}.
\tag{PC109.6}
\]

Set

\[
\varepsilon_{109}:=0.0015157,
\qquad
t_{109}:=C_{146}+\varepsilon_{109}.
\tag{PC109.7}
\]

At the right endpoint of (PC109.6),

\[
\delta_{109}
={{9\over2}\varepsilon_{109}-g\over2}
=0.002865325.
\tag{PC109.8}
\]

The exact-rational certificate
`research/verify_target_c_three_label_orbit_chamber_propagation.py` proves

\[
1.821029237951019<t_{109}<1.821029237995464,
\tag{PC109.9}
\]

\[
F_{t_{109}}(\delta_{109})<-5.2\times10^{-5},
\tag{PC109.10}
\]

and

\[
\partial_\delta F_{t_{109}}(\delta)>142
\qquad(0<\delta\le\delta_{109}).
\tag{PC109.11}
\]

Audited §171 also proves strict monotonicity in `t`, so no feasible Type-II limit can have `t<=t_109`. A non-load-bearing high-precision solve puts the unchanged-envelope root at

\[
\varepsilon_*=0.001515855755331\ldots,
\tag{PC109.12}
\]

leaving the safe decimal in (PC109.7) below the first zero.

