## 8. Current frontier

After TC109 the strongest scalar package on this branch is

```text
atomic train gain              0.00109
q-k                            > 1.82102923795 D
bounded exceptional faces f   >= 0.16745964347 D
J interface                    >= 2.49086781185 D
H correlated defect            >= 1.49566681711 D
chamber area surplus           >= 0.64764272961 D
rhombus count deficit          >= 0.74783340855 D
corrected residual upper cap   <= 2.89135974241 D
```

This is not a closure. Scalar optimization is no longer the main bottleneck. The low-residual hard corner now carries a linear family of flat pentagonal source objects. Their middles satisfy the exact local split proved on this branch:

- loaded flat middle -> contact degree exactly two -> one full unit of `s_B`;
- unloaded flat middle -> external contact stress is `O(flatness)` relative to the two through contacts, with the through weights asymptotically equal;
- unloaded degree four additionally creates three hidden `1+o(1)` noncontacts.

A closing theorem should exploit that defect-payment/stress-through dichotomy rather than further tune the scalar endpoint.

**Disposition:** proof-only propagation. C-II and Level I remain open.
